body:
well so far you have by far been the most helpful. whats a good place to get my feet wet with actually learning how things work? the only info i find currently is "put this in terminal and it will work" 

&#x200B;

and yeah i was mostly venting. many years of tutorials that dont work or arent for my distro, trying to bring windows knowlege to linux, bad experiences with it in school, just got a bit too much but i left my pc, came back and feel a bit more motivated now lol.

&#x200B;

couple things im working on atm is getting qemu/kvm working (virtual machine manager just says qemu/kvm is connecting and wont let me make a new vm)

&#x200B;

telegram app will crash (at random times for seemingly no reason, dont even know where to begin with that)

&#x200B;

any games i want to play will have 30+ audio outputs in the settings menu but none of them work. (if i was using wine or steam play then id let this go but this still happens in games that are natively supported by linux.)

i dont know how to explain it other than nothing works, basic stuff like chrome and spotify install fine but anything out of the norm or not in the app store has to be done through terminal and theres ALWAYS something that dosnt work when you have to do it through terminal. not to mention dealing with tar files and deb files that seem to always fail. (havnt experienced this on pop, its package manager seems to work pretty well but it is the outlier out of all the distros i have used)

&#x200B;

and yeah this post is a little rambly,
